Every clinician should consider a recommendation during a clinician-patient-relationship.
Every clinician-patient-relationship should have a shared-understanding.
Every clinician should consider a recommendation during a whole-person-approach.
If a clinician uses a whole-person-approach for a patient then the clinician should consider a physical-functioning for the patient and should consider a psychological-functioning for the patient.
If a clinician uses a whole-person-approach for a patient then the clinician should consider a support-need for the patient and should consider an expected-health-outcome for the patient and should consider a well-being for the patient.
If a clinician uses a whole-person-approach for a patient then the clinician should consider a home-environment for the patient and should consider a home-responsibility for the patient and should consider a work-responsibility for the patient.
Every recommendation relies on an emerging-evidence.
An emerging-evidence-example includes an observational-study-example and includes a limited-randomized-clinical-trial-example.
